    "title": "Blue-spotted salamander migration is on schedule in Marquette, experts say - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Julia Seitz ,\n8 hours ago MARQUETTE, Mich. (WLUC) - It’s blue-spotted salamander migration season in Marquette, and experts say the salamanders’ travel plans are on schedule. The Superior Watershed Partnership hasn’t seen any salamanders cross Peter White Drive on Presque Isle yet, but Special Projects Coordinator and Education Specialist Kathleen Henry says that’s normal. Their migration to vernal pools for reproduction is weather-dependent. She says previous data shows movement throughout March, April and May. Read full article\nRead in NewsBreak",
